    // We treat the residual as a cost function, but we want to avoid creating "orphans"
    // (bins with very little space that can't fit future items).

    // 2. Harmonic Class Penalization:
    // If post_residual is small (e.g., < 10), it becomes a "dead zone" unless it perfectly hits 0.
    if post_residual > 0 && post_residual < 10 {
